      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those critics are clinging to outdated economic models that assume labor scarcity will always guarantee wage stability. The cost of UBI must be weighed against the exponentially higher costs of mass unemployment, social instability, and healthcare crises resulting from economic collapse. Furthermore, the productivity gains from AI itself can fund UBI through new tax structures on automated capital, effectively shifting wealth from machines to people. Their resistance is rooted in protecting obsolete economic structures, not in sound fiscal planning.",
      "source": "target",
